// @reject: a module that never says what it exports. The grammar marks `#>`
// @reject: optional and said nothing about the omission, so the three engines
// @reject: filled the silence three ways: the tree-walker exported everything,
// @reject: the VM and the browser engine exported nothing, and `zymbol check`
// @reject: said `No errors or warnings` about a module whose every call dies at
// @reject: runtime in two engines of three (DM-27, REFERENCE.md L48).
// @reject: Decided 2026-09-04: a module declares its public surface. The rule
// @reject: lives in `zymbol-semantic` (E014), so all three engines inherit it
// @reject: and `check` sees it — the module file is refused wherever it is read.
// @reject: An empty `#> { }` is how a module says it exports nothing, out loud.
// @reject: It was free to decide: of every module in the corpus and in the six
// @reject: LDV applications, none omitted the block, so nothing depended on
// @reject: either default.
# 04_module_without_export_block_m {
    TOPE := 7

    privada() {
        <~ TOPE * 2
    }

    publica() {
        <~ privada()
    }
}
